spec: specs/di.md stage 3, redesigned (operator's go, 2026-09-09)

why: a module that opens infrastructure itself is invisible to the
  deployment — the demo opens okay-board.log and its manifest declares
  a port and no volume. The component that opens the thing is the one
  that knows the need; today it has nowhere to say it.

what: core — a Module carries FACTS beside its installer (a typed key
  with its own merge, stored in TMap; no deployment word in core),
  `declare`, and READINESS: a ready module (Module.value/ready) lets
  `and` apply the dependent right side eagerly, so facts are readable
  up to the first acquisition — after config, before infrastructure.
  okay-deploy — `needs`/`needsOf` over Module. Demo — the store
  declares its Volume; DemoDeploy derives needs from the app.

next: core first, watched at real call sites for the E10 trap
